.Dd August 30, 2026
.Dt PAPERSPLZ 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm papersplz , pplz
.Nd manage a local catalog of academic papers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -home Ar path
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
stores catalog-owned copies of papers together with human-readable JSON
metadata.
Each catalog is self-contained and can be moved as a directory.
.Nm pplz
is a shorter name for the same program.
.Pp
Most commands require a catalog selected with
.Fl -home
or
.Ev PAPERSPLZ_HOME .
The
.Cm init
command instead takes the new catalog path directly.
Paper and comment identifiers may be shortened to an unambiguous prefix.
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -home Ar path
Use the catalog at
.Ar path ,
overriding
.Ev PAPERSPLZ_HOME .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show top-level help.
Command groups and major commands also accept
.Fl -help .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init Ar path Fl -name Ar name Op Fl -description Ar text
Create a catalog.
.It Cm add Ar source Fl -title Ar title Op options
Import a local file or direct HTTP or HTTPS URL.
Options include repeatable
.Fl -author Ar name
and
.Fl -tag Ar tag ,
plus
.Fl -source Ar text .
.It Cm edit Ar paper Op options
Change supplied metadata fields.
Options are
.Fl -title ,
.Fl -author ,
.Fl -clear-authors ,
.Fl -source ,
and
.Fl -source-url .
.It Cm remove Ar paper Op Fl -yes
Remove a paper and its catalog-owned files.
Non-interactive use requires
.Fl -yes .
.It Cm show Ar paper Op Fl -json
Show paper metadata.
.It Cm path Ar paper
Print only the stored document path.
.It Cm open Ar paper
Open the stored document with the platform viewer.
.It Cm list Op options
List papers.
Options include
.Fl -tag ,
.Fl -author ,
.Fl -sort Cm title Ns | Ns Cm added Ns | Ns Cm author ,
.Fl -reverse ,
.Fl -limit ,
and
.Fl -json .
.It Cm info Op Fl -json
Show catalog metadata and counts.
.It Cm review Cm show Ar paper Op Fl -json
Show the paper review.
.It Cm review Cm set Ar paper Bro Ar text | Fl -file Ar file | - Brc
Set the paper review from text, a file, or standard input.
.It Cm review Cm edit Ar paper
Edit the review with
.Ev EDITOR .
.It Cm review Cm remove Ar paper
Remove the review.
.It Cm comment Cm add Ar paper Ar text
Add a comment.
.It Cm comment Cm list Ar paper Op Fl -json
List comments in creation order.
.It Cm comment Cm show Ar paper Ar comment Op Fl -json
Show a comment.
.It Cm comment Cm edit Ar paper Ar comment
Edit a comment with
.Ev EDITOR .
.It Cm comment Cm remove Ar paper Ar comment
Remove a comment.
.It Cm tag Cm add Ar paper Ar tag ...
Add tags to a paper.
.It Cm tag Cm remove Ar paper Ar tag ...
Remove tags from a paper.
.It Cm tag Cm list Ar paper Op Fl -json
List a paper's tags.
.It Cm tags Op Fl -json
List all catalog tags and usage counts.
.It Cm mark Bro Cm unread | reading | read Brc Ar paper
Set the conventional reading-status tag while preserving unrelated tags.
.It Cm relation Cm add Ar paper Ar type Ar other
Add a relationship.
.It Cm relation Cm list Ar paper Op Fl -json
List direct and derived relationships.
.It Cm relation Cm remove Ar paper Ar type Ar other
Remove a relationship.
Relationship types are
.Cm related-to ,
.Cm cites ,
.Cm cited-by ,
.Cm supersedes ,
and
.Cm superseded-by .
.It Cm search Ar term ... Op options
Search managed metadata using case-insensitive plain-text AND matching.
Options include
.Fl -tag ,
.Fl -author ,
and
.Fl -json .
.It Cm export Op Fl -json
Write all catalog-managed metadata as JSON.
Stored document contents are not included.
.It Cm doctor
Check catalog consistency without changing it.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PAPERSPLZ_HOME
.It Ev PAPERSPLZ_HOME
Catalog path used when
.Fl -home
is not supplied.
.It Ev EDITOR
Editor command used by review and comment editing.
No editor is guessed when this variable is unset.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa catalog.json
Catalog metadata at the catalog root.
.It Pa papers/
Paper records and catalog-owned document copies.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors and catalog or operation failures return a non-zero status.
Diagnostics are written to standard error; normal results are written to
standard output.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create and select a catalog:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pplz init "$HOME/papers" --name "My Papers"
export PAPERSPLZ_HOME="$HOME/papers"
.Ed
.Pp
Import and inspect a paper:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pplz add paper.pdf --title "Example Paper" --tag unread
pplz list
pplz show PAPER_ID
.Ed
.Pp
Mark a paper as being read and search its metadata:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pplz mark reading PAPER_ID
pplz search spectral sequence --tag reading
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr open 1
